Hi,

Do you have NAs in both observation and covariate data?
I used to have this issue when a given node consists only of NAs.
In order to test if this is the problem, you could replace the NAs in your covariate data by some value (e.g., covariate average, data imputation, ...).

I hope it helps you.

Cheers

